note Source: CPython Lib/statistics.py, _sum.
note _sum(data) -> (type, sum, count): a high-precision sum of numeric data as a fraction,
note with the type the result should be converted to and the count of items.

note GAP: reflection - Python groups data by type(x) and returns the class object itself.
note Scribe has no runtime type values and no `type of x`. A closed choice of the four numeric
note kinds Python's statistics module accepts stands in for an arbitrary numeric object, and a
note second choice names the kind to return.
choice Number
    Whole with value as an Int
    Float with value as a Float
    Ratio with value as a Fraction
    Exact_decimal with value as a Decimal

choice NumberKind
    Int_kind
    Float_kind
    Fraction_kind
    Decimal_kind

note UNCLEAR: the doc has Int, Nat and Money but never names a floating-point, rational or
note decimal type. Float, Fraction and Decimal are assumed to exist in a standard vocabulary.

note GAP: missing values used as a dictionary key - Python keys partials by denominator and
note uses None as the key for non-finite values (NaN, infinity). Scribe has no map type, and
note maybe values as keys are not discussed. The two roles are split: a list of
note (denominator, numerator) pairs plus a separate maybe for the non-finite total.
type Partial
    field denominator as a Nat
    field numerator as an Int

choice ExactRatio
    Finite with numerator as an Int and denominator as a Nat
    Not_finite with value as a Float

type SumResult
    field kind as a NumberKind
    field total as an ExactTotal
    field count as a Nat

choice ExactTotal
    Exact with value as a Fraction
    Special with value as a Float

to exact_ratio x
    given x is a Number
    produces an ExactRatio

to kind_of x
    given x is a Number
    produces a NumberKind

to coerce first and second
    given first is a NumberKind
    given second is a NumberKind
    produces a NumberKind
    fails with TypeError

to fraction_from numerator over denominator
    given numerator is an Int
    given denominator is a Nat
    produces a Fraction

to is_finite value
    given value is a Float
    produces a Bool

note GAP: allocation - the original builds a set and a dict. The doc says allocating operations
note name an Allocator in uses, but no example shows a collection being created or grown with
note one, so the allocator is declared and the growth sites do not mention it.
to sum_of data using memory
    given data is a List of Number
    given memory is an Allocator
    produces a SumResult
    fails with TypeError, OutOfMemory
    uses memory

    var count starts at 0
    note WORKAROUND: Python's set of types becomes a List with a membership test before adding.
    note UNCLEAR: the doc shows `append value to items of queue` (example 9) only for a field of
    note a record; appending to a local `var` list is assumed to be written the same way.
    var types starts at []
    var partials starts at []
    note UNCLEAR: `var special starts at nothing` gives no element type. The doc does not say
    note whether a var's type can be written or must be inferred from later `set` lines.
    var special starts at nothing

    note WORKAROUND: itertools.groupby(data, type) groups consecutive items of the same type; the
    note only use of the grouping is to add each type to a set, so a plain loop with a
    note membership check gives the same set.
    for each x in data
        let kind be kind_of x
        if kind is not in types
            append kind to types
        set count to count + 1
        choose exact_ratio x
            when Finite with numerator and denominator
                note WORKAROUND: partials.get(d, 0) + n on a dict becomes a linear search of a
                note list of records with a found flag, because Scribe has no map type and no
                note early-exit search expression.
                var found starts at false
                for each i from 0 until count of partials
                    let entry be item i of partials
                    if denominator of entry is denominator
                        note GAP: replacing one element of a list. The doc has `item i of items`
                        note for reading but no form for writing an element, so
                        note `set item i of partials to ...` is invented by analogy with
                        note `set balance of account to ...`.
                        note UNCLEAR: record construction syntax is not shown except in
                        note `an Order from cart and receipt with status Paid` (example 29).
                        note UNCLEAR: the field label `numerator` and the bound name `numerator`
                        note are the same word, so the parser must tell a label from a value by
                        note position alone.
                        set item i of partials to a Partial with denominator denominator and numerator numerator of entry + numerator
                        set found to true
                        stop
                if not found
                    append a Partial with denominator denominator and numerator numerator to partials
            when Not_finite with value
                note Python: partials[None] = partials.get(None, 0) + n, where n is a float
                note NaN or infinity. Adding a float to the int 0 keeps the float.
                choose special
                    when nothing
                        set special to some value
                    when some earlier
                        set special to some earlier + value

    note WORKAROUND: the dict lookup `None in partials` becomes a choose on the maybe.
    var total starts at Exact with value fraction_from 0 over 1
    choose special
        when some value
            note The original asserts the special total is not finite.
            note UNCLEAR: `expect` is shown only in headers and `assert` only inside a proof
            note block. Neither is shown as a run-time check in a body; `expect` is used here.
            expect not is_finite value
            set total to Special with value value
        when nothing
            var exact_sum starts at fraction_from 0 over 1
            for each entry in partials
                set exact_sum to exact_sum + fraction_from numerator of entry over denominator of entry
            set total to Exact with value exact_sum

    note WORKAROUND: reduce(_coerce, types, int) becomes an explicit fold loop starting from
    note Int_kind. The doc's comprehension form has no fold or reduce.
    var result_kind starts at Int_kind
    for each kind in types
        set result_kind to try coerce result_kind and kind
    give back a SumResult with kind result_kind and total total and count count
